From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iván Ruiz <iruizl2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:39:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2158/2160] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p64100-microsoft-denali: Drive
 the backlight from the PMK8550 PWM

The LCD Surface Pro 11 (LG LP129WT3 panel) takes its brightness from a
PWM signal, like the Surface Laptop 7 and the Surface Pro 12in. Its
TCON advertises eDP AUX brightness control and ACKs writes to the
brightness registers (DPCD 0x722/0x723), but ignores them: their value
reads back unchanged and the screen does not change, so the DP AUX
backlight that panel-edp registers without a backlight phandle has no
effect.

Describe a pwm-backlight on PMK8550 PWM channel 0, routed out of PMK8550
GPIO5 (func3) as on the Surface Laptop 7, and point the panel at it.
Brightness then follows the backlight device across its full range.

Fixes: 0d72ccaa1e84 ("arm64: dts: qcom: Add support for X1-based Surface Pro 11")
Assisted-by: LLM

---
 .../dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts    | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
index d96202e2a..e18444532 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
@@ -12,4 +12,28 @@ / {
 	model = "Microsoft Surface Pro 11th Edition (LCD)";
 	compatible = "microsoft,denali-lcd", "microsoft,denali",
 		     "qcom,x1p64100", "qcom,x1e80100";
+
+	backlight: backlight {
+		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
+		pwms = <&pmk8550_pwm 0 5000000>;
+		power-supply = <&vreg_edp_3p3>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&edp_bl_pwm>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&panel {
+	backlight = <&backlight>;
+};
+
+&pmk8550_gpios {
+	edp_bl_pwm: edp-bl-pwm-state {
+		pins = "gpio5";
+		function = "func3";
+	};
+};
+
+&pmk8550_pwm {
+	status = "okay";
 };
